# SentinelAI — Comprehensive Codebase Exploration & Technical Review

## 1. Architectural Overview

SentinelAI is an **incident-centered AI security copilot** that fuses browser telemetry, ML model inference, threat intelligence, and LLM-generated explanations into a unified incident-management pipeline. It comprises three deployable units:

```mermaid
graph TB
  subgraph "Browser Extension (MV3)"
    BG["Background Service Worker"]
    CS["Content Script"]
    POP["Popup UI"]
    OPT["Options Page"]
  end

  subgraph "FastAPI Backend"
    API["REST API (v1)"]
    TI["Threat Intel\n(VT/AbuseIPDB/PhishTank)"]
    PHI["DistilBERT\nPhishing Classifier"]
    IF["Isolation Forest\nAnomaly Detector"]
    TCE["Threat Correlation\nEngine"]
    RAG["RAG Service\n(pgvector)"]
    LLM["Gemini LLM"]
    MW["Middleware\n(Rate Limit, Logging, Errors)"]
  end

  subgraph "React Dashboard (Vite)"
    LP["Login Page"]
    DH["Dashboard Home"]
    IP["Incident Pages"]
    NP["Network Page"]
    DP["Devices Page"]
  end

  subgraph "PostgreSQL + pgvector"
    DB["9 Tables:\nusers, devices, sessions,\nevents, incidents, evidence,\nai_responses, threat_cache,\nplaybooks"]
  end

  BG -->|JWT + Events| API
  CS -->|Form submissions| BG
  POP -->|Phishing check| API
  DH -->|REST/JSON| API
  IP -->|REST/JSON| API
  API --> TI
  API --> PHI
  API --> IF
  TI --> TCE
  PHI --> TCE
  IF --> TCE
  TCE --> RAG
  RAG --> LLM
  TCE --> DB
  LLM --> DB
```

### Core Pipeline (the "Incident Lifecycle")

Every event flows through a **13-step pipeline** defined in [incident_service.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/services/incident_service.py):

1. **Extension** observes browser events (navigation, downloads, form submission)
2. **Events API** ingests telemetry → persists `Event` row
3. **Threat Intelligence** lookups (VirusTotal, AbuseIPDB, PhishTank — cached in `threat_cache`)
4. **DistilBERT** classifies URLs/text as phishing or legitimate
5. **Isolation Forest** scores network flows for anomalousness
6. **Signal generation** — typed `Signal` objects with name, score, and reason
7. **Threat Correlation Engine** fuses signals via noisy-OR into an `Incident`
8. **MITRE ATT&CK mapping** from signals → technique IDs
9. **RAG retrieval** — cosine similarity over playbook embeddings (pgvector)
10. **Gemini LLM** generates plain-English summary + numbered remediation
11. **Dashboard** renders the incident with evidence, AI explanation, and MITRE chips

