## 4. Prioritized Weaknesses & Risks

### 🔴 Critical

| # | Issue | Location | Impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| **S1** | **No password strength validation on registration** | [auth_service.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/services/auth_service.py#L32-L42) | Any password (even `"a"`) is accepted; only client-side `minLength=8` exists |
| **S2** | **JWT tokens are never invalidated** | [security.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/core/security.py) | No token blocklist/revocation on logout; compromised tokens remain valid until expiry (24h access, 7d refresh) |
| **S3** | **CORS wildcard `allow_methods=["*"]`, `allow_headers=["*"]`** | [main.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/main.py#L48-L55) | Overly permissive — DELETE/PUT are exposed even though not all routes use them |
| **S4** | **No input sanitization on `payload_json` (JSONB)** | [event.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/models/event.py#L54) | Arbitrary JSON is stored; no size limit or schema validation — potential for storage abuse or XSS if rendered unsanitized in the dashboard |
| **S5** | **Rate limiter is per-IP only, no per-user limiting** | [rate_limit.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/middleware/rate_limit.py) | All authenticated users behind the same NAT share a single IP bucket; a single malicious user can exhaust it |

### 🟠 High

| # | Issue | Location | Impact |
|---|---|---|---|
| **H1** | **Synchronous ML inference on the request path** | [phishing_model.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/ml/phishing_model.py#L160-L188), [incident_service.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/services/incident_service.py#L63-L76) | DistilBERT and Isolation Forest run synchronously in the async event loop, blocking all concurrent requests during inference (~50-200ms per URL) |
| **H2** | **No pagination/throttle on event batch ingestion** | [events.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/api/v1/events.py#L58-L96) | A single batch request can contain unlimited events, each triggering the full pipeline (ML + threat intel + LLM) — trivial DoS vector |
| **H3** | **`asyncio.create_task` for replay without lifecycle management** | [network_service.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/services/network_service.py#L99-L101) | Fire-and-forget task; no cancellation, no status tracking, no error recovery. Task reference is dropped immediately |
| **H4** | **LLM calls are synchronous (blocking the event loop)** | [llm_service.py](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/backend/app/services/llm_service.py#L96) | `client.models.generate_content()` is a sync call inside an async pipeline — blocks the entire server for 1-5 seconds per incident |
| **H5** | **No RBAC / user roles** | Entire auth system | Every user has identical permissions; no admin vs. analyst vs. viewer roles |
| **H6** | **Dashboard lacks real-time updates** | [useDashboard.ts](file:///e:/vatsal/sentinelai/dashboard/src/hooks/useDashboard.ts) | Dashboard uses polling (or one-shot fetch), not WebSocket/SSE — incidents don't appear until the user manually refreshes or navigates |

