### Step-by-step

#### 1. PostgreSQL + pgvector

**Windows (native)**:
```powershell
# Download and install PostgreSQL 16 from https://www.postgresql.org/download/windows/
# During installation, note the port (default 5432) and superuser password

# After installation, open pgAdmin or psql:
psql -U postgres

# In psql:
CREATE ROLE sentinelai WITH LOGIN PASSWORD 'sentinelai';
CREATE DATABASE sentinelai OWNER sentinelai;
\c sentinelai
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;
\q
```

**WSL2**:
```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y postgresql-16 postgresql-16-pgvector
sudo service postgresql start
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE ROLE sentinelai WITH LOGIN PASSWORD 'sentinelai';"
sudo -u postgres psql -c "CREATE DATABASE sentinelai OWNER sentinelai;"
sudo -u postgres psql -d sentinelai -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;"
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **pgvector** must be installed as a PostgreSQL extension. On Windows, you may need to install it manually — download from [pgvector releases](https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector/releases) and follow the Windows instructions. On WSL2/Linux, `postgresql-16-pgvector` is the package to install.

