### Common Setup Issues

| Issue | Fix |
|---|---|
| `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'psycopg2'` | Install `pip install psycopg2-binary` (should be in requirements.txt already) |
| `could not translate host name "localhost" to address` | Ensure PostgreSQL is running and accepting connections on port 5432 |
| `extension vector is not available` | Install pgvector: on Windows follow [manual build instructions](https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector#windows), on Linux install `postgresql-16-pgvector` |
| `torch` import fails | Install torch separately before `requirements.txt` — see the comment in requirements.txt |
| Alembic migration fails | Ensure `DATABASE_URL_SYNC` in `.env` uses `postgresql+psycopg2://` (sync driver) |
| Dashboard shows "Unable to load dashboard" | Backend must be running on port 8000; check `.env` in dashboard says `VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1` |
| Extension API calls fail | Open extension Options page → verify API URL is `http://localhost:8000/api/v1` |

